{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>A half shekel.</b> To atone for the half of the day on which they sinned, as they said in tractate Shabbat, chapter רבי עקיבא בושש בא. And the shekel is twenty gerah — thus half of it is ten, to atone for the Ten Commandments that they transgressed. And it is stated in Zevachim, chapter רבי ישמעאל אומר: Five fingers of the right hand of the Holy One, blessed be He — all of them are for the unification of redemption. With the little finger He showed Noah to make the ark, as it is said: ״וזה אשר תעשה אותה״. The second one — when He struck Egypt, as it is said: ״אצבע אלהים הוא״. The third, which is a cubit — concerning it is written: ״והלוחות כתובים באצבע אלהים״. The fourth, which is adjacent to the thumb — He showed Moses the moon in its size. He showed him the half shekel, as it is said: ״זה יתנו״. And with the entire hand the Holy One, blessed be He, is destined to cut down and destroy the children of Ishmael and the children of Aram, as it is said: ״תרום ידך על צריך וכל אויביך יכרתו״."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The phrase 'בגודל' is rendered 'in its size' (referring to the moon), though it could conceivably relate to the thumb (גודל) mentioned in the preceding phrase; the Hebrew is ambiguous."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:22.096427336Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}